    {
      "id": "v1/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top1/r00/bootstrap",
      "evidence_sha256": "123819e8b8ea0d5d7f4dd6ffdd293b8fe213c698189fbce4177aca6a96bb0eb0",
      "assessment": "The bootstrap read a real R0 with Mean 4.1724, 100 valid molecules and very small, mostly unclipped guidance. Its archived failed response proposed [8,8,8,8], [9,7,5,4], [4,5,7,8], and [6,6,6,6] outside the existing move contract; the repaired request exposed the limits and produced legal single-window tests. However H2 calls interval 1 the least actuated although interval 2 has lower measured displacement, and infers low-score pose errors without joining geometry to score strata.",
      "decision_update": "Preserve the actual-action contract and require a zero-based interval/start/end/old/new action table. At bootstrap, describe low score versus geometric residual as separate observations until a candidate-level association is checked. H1-H4 are exploratory timing contrasts, not four established mechanisms; subsequent R1 means were all below R0 for this teacher.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "Low displacement and absent clipping do not prove useful unused affinity control; the R1 results contradict an automatic upward Mean forecast. The old failed response was never sampled and one API token receipt is missing, so its sampling outcome and exact cost cannot be supplied. The small archived transport repair did not alter the reward or frozen skill.",
