    {
      "id": "v1/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top1/r01/G2",
      "evidence_sha256": "4c4250686e692c41927ce5adf0bc8ca0df5859ca92ff36073c58eb58cf9691dc",
      "assessment": "R1 G2 saw Mean 4.16124 versus 4.17240, with Q2 and Q4 losses, then proposed H1 [5,5,6,5] and H2 [5,6,5,6]. The requests include endpoint geometry at step 50 and interval comparisons. The final diagnosis calls the intervention effectively a no-op despite interval-1 inside displacement increasing from about 0.000421 to 0.000504 Angstrom; it also misreports the paired win direction and mixes zero-based and one-based interval language.",
      "decision_update": "Distinguish small absolute control from an unexecuted or ineffective amplitude change. State comparison as named B minus A and cross-check against both population means before interpreting win rate. Describe H1 as a two-window relocation whose components are not individually identified, and H2 as a terminal increment on the inherited schedule.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "The small loss is dominated by a few candidates, but no repeated independent randomness was used to estimate a noise band. Geometry headroom at step 50 does not establish affinity headroom or justify treating every weak response as permission to escalate another interval.",
