      "assessment": "R1 G4 has two concrete reasoning errors. It invents a symmetric +0.7202/-0.7202 pair by combining opposite-direction reports of one loss, although the latest-minus-incumbent maximum is only +0.0152. It labels the changed third tick as steps 26-50 and describes H2 [5,6,4,5] as an earliest-window increment, although its array changes steps 26-50. H1 [5,5,5,5] is a legal reversion, and all actual sampled results remain valid.",
      "decision_update": "Require one canonical sign for narrative comparisons and distinguish a maximum paired difference from population Best. Before submission, derive the textual action from the actual tick-array difference and supplied interval metadata. A reverse comparison is the same observation with reversed sign, never independent support or a cancelling second molecule.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "The legal arrays were executed as written; this is an interpretation/action-description mismatch, not proof that the sampler used wrong intervals. Reverting to the old tick vector from selected mixed parents need not reproduce the original population. Best was effectively unchanged, so this case does not show upper-tail improvement.",
